            <ArticleTitle>Cholesterol lowering in the elderly population. Coordinating Committee of the National Cholesterol Education Program.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1670-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence of coronary heart disease (CHD) peaks in the elderly population. In secondary and primary prevention trials, cholesterol-lowering therapy reduces risk for CHD in both older and younger participants. This benefit, therefore, can be extended to the elderly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
